  "steps": [
    "New-script graph selection, field location and collapse/reopen preserve the exact reviewed source and dirty state. Real key edits regenerate source; an incomplete key removes all stale graph items. Cancelling writes no author files.",
    "The re-edit graph retains all three states including an isolated state, five transitions, a reverse direction, a self-loop and three triggers sharing a route. Selecting that route selects exactly its three transitions; explicit Locate focuses the corresponding real field without revoking the approved source.",
    "An invalid state clears every graph node and transition; a detached Locate button cannot focus a replacement row. Repair restores the graph. Collapse and Chinese/English/Japanese changes preserve the source review, exact graph/input nodes, input focus and text selection. At390px only the bounded graph canvas scrolls horizontally. Cancel leaves source and all author files unchanged.",
    "A deliberate event change follows Check → reviewed source → Apply to the unsaved draft → ordinary Save. The graph reopens both the dirty draft and the saved TXT. Only that TXT changes; registration, identity, bindings and every other author file remain unchanged."
  ],
